  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25 or below) and historical price trends show downward momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (e.g., +0.50) and price has recently been trending upward — anticipate reversal.",
    "Lag correction: if model forecasts are consistently ahead of true outcomes by 1-2 days, reduce forecast by 3-5% for the next day’s prediction.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment spikes — use 3-day rolling average sentiment to smooth out noise before adjusting forecasts."
  ]
}
